neural-render.jpeg
# raw Claude-Design dump is ignored; keep only the build inputs the bundle needs.
#
# ALLOW BY CONVENTION, NOT BY FILENAME (v1.77.0). This used to name five files
# explicitly, which meant every NEW build input was silently ignored: the existing
# challenge-*.src.js / challenge-*.css / sound.src.js survive only because someone
# force-added them. A new file (e.g. neural/src/lists.src.js) would be absent from
# CI's checkout, so `node neural/build/build.mjs` would either error or quietly ship
# a bundle missing the feature — green locally, broken in production.
#
# The `.src.` infix and `.css` are the markers of a build input (build.mjs reads
# exactly these); a raw design dump uses plain names (App.jsx, index.js) and stays
# ignored. Verify any new file with: git check-ignore -v neural/src/<file>
neural/src/*
!neural/src/*.src.js
!neural/src/*.src.jsx
!neural/src/*.css
!neural/src/xdc-template.html
!neural/src/helmet.html
!neural/src/props.json
!neural/src/technique-content.js

# Playwright journey-suite artifacts (e2e/gallery keyframes are regenerated per run)
e2e/report/
e2e/report-gen/
e2e/test-results/
test-results/
e2e/gallery/

# Paired-debugging sessions (journals + shared-browser profile/pids are per-session scratch)
e2e/paired/

# Dev snapshot captures (written by scripts/dev-serve.mjs; see CLAUDE.md "Dev Snapshots").
# Only this subdir — the rest of tests/artifacts/ is tracked.
tests/artifacts/snapshots/
# Replay artifacts: run outputs of scripts/triple_replay.sh + the replay-digest spec. Regenerable,
# per-run, and only meaningful compared against each other within one invocation.
tests/artifacts/triple_replay/
tests/artifacts/replay/
# Belt-meter design iteration screenshots (regenerable from any build via the belt-meter spec)
tests/artifacts/belt/
# Pane-and-chrome polish screenshots + red-run log (regenerable via the pane-chrome spec)
tests/artifacts/chrome/
node_modules/

# Transient local-agent coordination notes (this checkout only; repo is public)
HANDOFF.md
